{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-algebraic-filter-classification","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:algebraic-filter-classification","kind":"proposition","title":"Fermion--boson classification by commutator with curvature","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-q-harmonic-basis-brane"],"examples":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-q-harmonic-basis-brane","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-weight-space-decomposition","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-algebraic-filter","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-distributional-connection"],"tags":["fermion","boson","algebraic-filter","curvature","classification"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Torsion.algebraic_filter_classification","text":"algebraic-filter-classification.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/algebraic-filter-classification.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:algebraic-filter-classification\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">F_A</code> be the curvature of the substrate parameter (<a href=\"#def:substrate-parameter\">substrate parameter</a>) and let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\alpha</code> be a harmonic <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">1</code>-form in the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-harmonic basis on branes (<a href=\"#rem:q-harmonic-basis-brane\">q-harmonic basis</a>).</p>\n<p>The commutator <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">[F_A, \\alpha]</code> classifies <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\alpha</code> into exactly one of two types:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Fermionic (matter).</strong> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">[F_A, \\alpha] \\neq 0</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Bosonic (radiation).</strong> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">[F_A, \\alpha] = 0</code>.</li>\n</ol>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/algebraic-filter-classification.md","leanStatus":"proved","heading":"Proposition","number":"5.8.4"}
